  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership for technology innovation in the management of water hyacinth, Managed aquifer recharge and livestock resource management in the ASALs for climate change mitigation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business Finland have discussed with the UNIDO Kenya Country Office on three offerings for potential partnership as follows: - 1.Utilization of water Hyacinth an invasive species in Lake Victoria as an economic resource.  Water hyacinth, an invasive species around Lake Victoria and also globally is native to the South American continent and causes multi-faceted problems # environmental, economic and social. A water hyacinth infestation is difficult to destroy and is seldom totally eradicated. Instead, it must be continually managed. In Lake Victoria, water hyacinths increased rapidly between 1992#1998, were greatly reduced by 2001 through various management techniques that included hyacinth eating insect controls and beach cleanups but have since resurged.  Business Finland in partnership with UNIDO and other actors is proposing to pilot a project that promotes the harvesting and the utilization of the hyacinth biomass as an economically beneficial resource. The Finnish partnership will pilot innovative technology for harvesting and processing the water hyacinth into an array of products including green energy generation. A research component of the project shall focus on the production of biochar, and biogas, pelleting, briquetting and the use of fertilizers produced from biochar and digestate.  2. Climate cha</narrative>
  </description>
